WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.638
Face swaps replace or blend a face in an image or video.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:10.022
Lip-sync manipulation changes mouth movement to match different audio.

00:00:10.022 --> 00:00:13.990
Voice cloning synthesizes speech that resembles a speaker.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:19.627
Each can be used with real footage, generated scenes, or edited recordings.

00:00:19.627 --> 00:00:25.683
AI-generated images can depict entirely fictional scenes or modify parts of real images.

00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:30.903
AI-generated video can create motion from prompts or animate still images.

00:00:30.903 --> 00:00:36.958
Quality varies, and visible artifacts are becoming less dependable as generation systems improve.

00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:43.013
Synthetic documents and screenshots can imitate interfaces, messages, invoices, headlines, or official forms.

00:00:43.013 --> 00:00:49.903
Their apparent structure may persuade viewers even when no underlying transaction, page, or record exists.

00:00:49.903 --> 00:00:54.288
Verification should seek the original system or authoritative record.

00:00:54.288 --> 00:00:59.508
Staged media is real media arranged to create a false impression.

00:00:59.508 --> 00:01:06.399
Miscontextualized media is genuine but presented with an incorrect date, place, identity, or event description.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:12.872
These cases can be as harmful as generated content and may survive visual-deepfake checks.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.168
Hybrid manipulation combines methods.

00:01:15.168 --> 00:01:22.059
Real video may contain generated audio, edited timing, removed objects, misleading captions, and synthetic frames.

00:01:22.059 --> 00:01:28.949
Labels should describe the supported finding rather than force every case into a single category.

00:01:28.949 --> 00:01:33.334
Classifying the media is only part of the task.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:45.653
Analysts must evaluate the associated claim: who published it, what it asserts, how it spread, what independent records exist, and what consequence follows if the claim is accepted.
